      "lotl": {
        "label": "What's Going On With the Leafs",
        "body": "A new front office has the Leafs in a hard reset, and the noise is real - not the fake kind that fills July. <strong>Toronto made Gavin McKenna the No. 1 pick in the 2026 NHL Draft</strong>, a franchise-altering swing that gives Auston Matthews the kind of young talent Connor McDavid and Zach Hyman are already praising as a fitting apprentice. The Leafs sit 8th in the Atlantic at 78 points, but that number belongs to a finished season; what matters now is how John Chayka shapes the roster around the rookie and the cap. Mitch Marner's agent saying he was \"never protected\" only sharpens the edges of this summer, and the sign-and-trade for Darren Raddysh shows the churn has started. <strong>Watch whether the Leafs keep adding support pieces - or save their muscle for one more major move.</strong>",
        "updated": "Updated July 28, 2026"
      },
