      "lotl": {
        "label": "What's Going On With the Jays",
        "body": "A season that has spent too much time in the ditch got a small, necessary lift Monday night. <strong>The Blue Jays edged the Nationals 3-2</strong>, with Luis Urías supplying the punch and Myles Straw chipping in a double and an RBI single as Toronto moved to 49-58 and held fifth in the AL East. That is not contender territory - not with a minus-4.5 mark and 14 games back - but it is at least a club showing a pulse after dropping two of three to Boston. Max Scherzer's return to Washington was part of the night's theater, and Shane Bieber gets the ball Tuesday as Toronto tries to stack wins for once. <strong>Watch Bieber's start at 6:45 p.m. ET and see whether the Jays can turn one good night into an actual run.</strong>",
        "updated": "Updated July 28, 2026"
