        "body": "A summer that should have been about quiet pruning has turned into a circus of old names and big swings. <strong>The Kawhi Leonard trade is on hold as the NBA investigates the Clippers' reported cap circumvention</strong>, and that delay hangs over everything Toronto does next. The Raptors sit at 3rd in the Atlantic Division, with the finished 46-36 record only a backdrop now; the real question is how much ceiling they can buy with the rest of the roster. Scottie Barnes remains the hinge, but the louder story is whether Toronto keeps chasing veteran firepower - DeMar DeRozan is suddenly back in the conversation, and Stephen Curry whispers only sharpen the intrigue. The Kyle Lowry trade tree keeps paying dividends in memory if not in certainty. <strong>What matters now is whether Toronto turns cap room and its final roster spots into one more real difference-maker.</strong>",
